# The uv release that easy-installer.bat bootstraps when uv is missing, and the SHA-256 of that release's installer
# scripts. Single source of truth: scripts/install-uv.sh (Linux/macOS/WSL/Git Bash) and scripts/install-uv.ps1
# (Windows) both read this file; the installer is downloaded to a file, verified against these digests and only
# then run. It is never piped into a shell.
#
# The digests are the `digest` field GitHub publishes for the release assets
#   https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/releases/tag/<UV_VERSION>   (uv-installer.sh, uv-installer.ps1)
# To move to a newer uv: change UV_VERSION and both digests together (e.g. with
#   gh api repos/astral-sh/uv/releases/tags/<version> --jq '.assets[] | select(.name|test("installer")) | [.name,.digest]'
# ) and let CI's `installer` job confirm. CI or a one-off run can override without editing this file by setting
# AGFLOW_UV_VERSION together with AGFLOW_UV_INSTALLER_SHA256.
UV_VERSION=0.12.9
UV_SH_SHA256=222e006c0fe4a0d793031833e469b21df72311f4e3526ffecca0e19e6dfabc32
UV_PS1_SHA256=69de475bf929f1ac248efb5a85189177a45517e2346cd68762bde453fec10a6b
